course: dictionary
lesson: 15965
title: Untruthful: not telling the truth
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Untruthful means not telling the truth. It is a softer, more formal word than «lying» or «a liar», and you often meet it in school reports and stories about honesty. «Ben gave an untruthful answer when Mum asked about the cake.» The clue is answer: Ben said something that was not true.
explain: Untruthful can describe a person, or a statement that is not true. «The advert was untruthful: the phone did not really last for a week.» Here the advert is the thing that is not telling the truth. Ask yourself: is the word describing a person or a statement?
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If «not telling the truth» still makes sense in place of untruthful, you have got it. The adverb untruthfully works the same way: «She answered untruthfully» means she answered without telling the truth.
fact: Untruthful means not telling the truth; lying.
fact: Untruthful can also describe a statement that is not true.
fact: The adverb untruthfully means in a way that does not tell the truth.
fact: «Untruthful» is a softer, more formal word than «lying» or «a liar».
fact: In safety, adverts or online messages may be untruthful, so check before you trust them.
exercise: «Ben gave an untruthful answer when Mum asked about the cake.» What does untruthful mean here? | Very quiet | Happy and pleased | *Not telling the truth | Hungry for cake
exercise: «The advert was untruthful: the phone did not really last for a week.» What does untruthful suggest about the advert? | It was made of paper | It was printed in colour | It was very long | *It said things that were not true
exercise: A teacher says a student's story was untruthful, not a lie. Why might a teacher choose untruthful? | It means very funny | *It is a softer, more formal word | It is a longer word for happy | It means the same as hungry
test: «She answered untruthfully when asked where she had been.» How did she answer? | *Without telling the truth | Loudly and happily | Honestly and clearly | Quickly, in rhyme
test: «Do not trust every online message; some of them are untruthful.» What does untruthful mean in this message? | *Not true | Full of pictures | Sent by a teacher | Written in capital letters
exam: «The witness was untruthful, so the judge did not believe her.» What is the best meaning of untruthful here? | Honest and kind | Tired from a long trial | *Not telling the truth | Late for court
